@startuml
left to right direction

title Use Case Diagram for AI-Powered Analysis & Insights System

rectangle "System" {
  usecase "CFR001: View Financial Insights Dashboard" as CFR001
  usecase "SAFR001: Manage Analysis Parameters" as SAFR001
  usecase "FAFR002: View Client Intervention Alerts" as FAFR002
  usecase "CFR004: Receive Personalized Recommendations" as CFR004
  usecase "CFR005: Manage Recommendation Preferences" as CFR005
  usecase "SAFR007: Generate Investment Opportunity Analysis" as SAFR007
  usecase "SFR013: Generate Client Alerts Based on Predefined Conditions" as SFR013
  usecase "CFR006: View Spending Limit Alerts" as CFR006
  usecase "SAFR008: Request Anomaly Transaction Alerts from AI Component" as SAFR008
  usecase "SFR009: Find Contextualized News Relevant to Portfolio" as SFR009
  usecase "CFR012: Manage Financial Goals Tracking" as CFR012
  usecase "AIFR003: Generate Spending Limit Alerts for Users" as AIFR003

  actor Client as c1
  client --> CFR001 : View financial insights dashboard\nConsolidates data from various sources.\nProvides a comprehensive view of financial health.
  
  SysAdmin as sas 
  sas --> SAFR001 : Manage analysis parameters for AI system to ensure accuracy and compliance with regulations like Basel III.

  FAFR002: View client intervention alerts when the system detects patterns requiring professional attention. This is done by Financial Advisors (FA) through their access.
  
  CFR004: Receive personalized recommendations aligned with financial profile and goals.\nOptimizes strategies, investment portfolios based on user data.
  
  CFR005: Manage personalization preferences to ensure relevance of insights per KYC-defined risk tolerance. This is a client action affecting system output.

  SAFR007: Generate investment opportunity analyses for clients by evaluating against their risk profiles and financial goals.\nThis use case involves the AI system (AIFR) processing requests from the system component.
  
  SFR013: Trigger alerts when conditions are met, such as exceeding spending limits or market downturns. This is a system-to-client communication.

  CFR006: View spending limit alerts to control budget.\nClient receives notifications if they exceed pre-set thresholds in specific categories (e.g., groceries).

  SAFR008: Request anomaly transaction alerts from the AI component for fraud detection, adhering to AML regulations. This is a system-level activity.

  SFR009: Find contextualized news related to client's portfolio.\nExtracts and provides relevant financial articles impacting investments.
  
  CFR012: Track progress towards financial goals set by clients.\nHelps in monitoring achievements over time, adjusting strategies as needed. This is a client action affecting system data.

  AIFR003: Generate spending limit alerts when user exceeds defined thresholds for specific categories (e.g., luxury goods). The AI component automates this based on historical and real-time data.
  
}

@enduml